It's actually surprisingly difficult to fix this particular interface
problem. At the point in the code where the direction is requested, the
code no longer knows how to cancel casting a spell. I tried to fix it in
AceHack by repeatedly asking for a direction in a loop until a valid
direction was available, but this had its own problems (e.g. if there
was a hangup at the spell direction prompt).

This is currently unfixed in NetHack 4, IIRC (unless one of the other
developers has fixed it already), although I'm planning to fix it when I
come up with a good fix. Probably the best would be to rearrange the
code so that cancelling spellcasting at the direction prompt is
possible; I can't think of any particular way to abuse that.

